build: 2026-06-26 v10.76.31 (rPPG octave-drift guard + faster healthy-confirm)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.30. Two stability fixes.
  1) rPPG octave-drift guard (#6): the pulse rate could slowly drift to half (or
     double) the true value over a minute — each window stepping just inside the old
     guard's band so it never tripped. Now the raw window rate is octave-corrected
     (×2 / ×0.5, an octave error is exactly a factor of two) against the octave-robust
     autocorrelation fundamental, only when a confident periodicity says we're a full
     octave off — never touching a genuine heart-rate change. Applied at the source so
     the median/EMA smoothing then works on correct values. Pure + unit-tested.
  2) Self-healing confirm: a launch is now marked healthy at END OF STARTUP (core
     ready) instead of after a fixed 4 s. It still covers the whole risky startup
     (graph build · voice attach · engine start), but quitting the app fast — e.g. to
     read the diagnostics log — no longer risks a spurious Safe Mode on the next launch.
  Diagnostics log of a healthy launch now reads: launch → init done → startup 1/4 →
  2/4 → 3/4 → 3/4 OK → 4/4 core ready → confirmed healthy.
  Test: 10.76.31 launches? Diagnostics shows the full sequence incl. "confirmed
  healthy". rPPG: finger on lens+flash → the BPM should hold its octave (no slow
  halving) over a minute.
